## 4. Testing by Component Type

### 4.1 Server Components

**Testing Server Components** (Next.js App Router):

```typescript
import { render, screen, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react'
import { Header } from '@/components/layout/header'

// Mock server-side data fetching
jest.mock('@/lib/aem/aem-client', () => ({
  getHeaderContent: jest.fn(),
}))

test('server component renders with data', async () => {
  const mockData = {
    logo: { title: 'Logo', Image: { _path: '/logo.png' } },
    topicNavigation1: { title: 'Home', path: '/' },
  }
  
  ;(getHeaderContent as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(mockData)
  
  render(<Header />)
  
  // Wait for async data
  await waitFor(() => {
    expect(screen.getByText('Home')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })
})
```

**Suspense Boundaries**:

```typescript
test('shows fallback while loading', () => {
  (getHeaderContent as jest.Mock).mockImplementation(
    () => new Promise(() => {}) // Never resolves
  )
  
  render(<Header />)
  
  // Verify fallback is shown
  expect(screen.getByLabelText('Loading header')).toBeInTheDocument()
})
```

**Error Boundaries**:

```typescript
test('handles error gracefully', async () => {
  const consoleErrorSpy = jest.spyOn(console, 'error').mockImplementation()
  
  (getHeaderContent as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(new Error('Failed'))
  
  render(<Header />)
  
  await waitFor(() => {
    expect(screen.getByText(/error/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
  })
  
  consoleErrorSpy.mockRestore()
})
```

